{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Measured from the field the policy names — gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 23.97 km, not the rounded 24.0 km convenience copy on the trip record — the excess over the booked optimal of 18.0 km is 5.97 km, or 33.17%. That clears the establishment gate in POL-RD-01 (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km; both tests pass on the trace figure), but it falls well short of the materiality gate: the excess is neither greater than 50% of the optimal distance nor greater than 8.0 km absolute. This is an established but ordinary deviation, and the materiality consequences do not attach.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the deviation is not material, POL-RD-06 is not engaged: there is no basis for the FULL_REFUND uplift in limb (b) of that clause and none for the driver-conduct referral in limb (c). Even if the profile check is run, no pattern is established on the only two counters POL-RD-06 and POL-GEN-01 permit: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1, below the threshold of 3, and 1 divided by completed_trips_90d of 412 is 0.0024, far below the 0.05 ratio. Limbs (a) to (c) all fail.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The recomputation runs on the multiplier recorded on the fare breakdown, and fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier is 1.6 — a figure the rider expressly accepts in the claim. Surge applies to the base, distance and time lines only: (3.80 + 0.75 x 18.0 + 0.28 x 30.0) x 1.6 = 41.12, plus the 0.80 platform fee and the 2.50 Kim Keat Link gantry that lies on the optimal route, giving a recomputed fare of 44.42. The surge uplift is therefore properly part of the comparison figure and is not stripped out of it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.surged_distance_and_time",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's \"$4.50 of ERP\" is not a sum that can be refunded on top of the recomputation. Only the 2.00 charged at the PIE (Adam Rd towards Tuas) gantry sits off the optimal route; the 2.50 at PIE (Kim Keat Link) carries on_optimal_route true and is properly chargeable, and it is already carried inside the 44.42 recomputed fare. The off-route 2.00 is itself already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund, because the recomputed fare includes only gantries lying on the optimal route — adding it again would double-count it, which POL-RD-09(1) expressly forbids. POL-RD-09(2) does not open a separate pass-through refund here because nothing is exonerated under POL-RD-03.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114", "EV-GPS-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither billed gantry is a phantom line, so no standalone billing-integrity refund arises under POL-RD-09(4). The trace passes within 0 m of the Kim Keat Link gantry and within 8.76 m of the Adam Rd gantry — both far inside the 250 m match the clause applies — and no airport surcharge appears anywhere on this trip. The two artifacts carrying this are COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so no admissibility discount applies to the finding.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00114", "EV-FARE-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[1].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arithmetic therefore lands at a refund of 13.68, rounded up to 13.70: charged_total of 58.10 less recomputed_fare of 44.42. That is not de minimis — it is well above the 0.50 floor under POL-RD-02 — and it is 23.5% of charged_total, far below the 90% share at which a partial converts to a full refund. The outcome the policy produces is a PARTIAL_REFUND of 13.70 against the 15.00 contested, on the separate lines charged_total 58.10, recomputed_fare 44.42, refund 13.70.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's congestion explanation cannot be certified on this record and I do not press it as an exoneration. The bundle's only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-00114-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so the POL-RD-03 comparison — a named segment the optimal route traverses, an overlapping validity window, and a route leaving and rejoining the corridor — cannot be run at all, and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 a congestion assertion naming no advisory carries no weight and supplies no adjusted optimal. No other exculpatory limb is open either: the chat log records a rider query, not a rider instruction, and carries no waypoint_hint (POL-RD-04); no pickup or dropoff amendment exists (POL-RD-05); the fare model is METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE (POL-RD-11); and the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12). The deviation stands at the measured figure and the case is decided on the arithmetic.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00114-01", "EV-CHAT-00114", "EV-TRIP-00114", "EV-FARE-00114"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-13"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 13.70,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider — your Bugis–Jurong East trip of 7 August 2026, billed at $58.10, is partly refunded. The route deviation is confirmed on the trip's own evidence: the GPS trace measures 23.97 km against the booked optimal route of 18.00 km, an excess of 5.97 km, or 33.17%. That clears the POL-RD-01 establishment gate (more than 20% of optimal and more than 0.8 km absolute), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not a MATERIAL deviation, because 33.17% is below the 50% gate and 5.97 km is below the 8.0 km gate.\n\nDriver — your explanation that the AYE was crawling and you went up and over on the PIE is not certified on this record. There is no traffic advisory on file for this trip: EV-ADVIS-00114-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. With no advisory, the POL-RD-03 comparison (a named segment the optimal route traverses, an overlapping validity window, and a route leaving and rejoining the corridor) cannot be run; under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 your uncited congestion assertion carries no weight and supplies no adjusted optimal route. This does not escalate the case: you named no advisory evidence ID (your statement says 'No advisory that I know of'), so POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged, and POL-RD-13(1) directs that the case be decided on the arithmetic. No other exculpatory limb is open — the chat log records a rider query and your reply 'AYE jam boss, this way faster', but no rider instruction to take a particular road and no waypoint (POL-RD-04); no pickup or dropoff was amended (POL-RD-05); the fare is METERED, not upfront (POL-RD-11); and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12).\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, run on the fare breakdown: base $3.80 + distance (0.75 × 18.00 km = $13.50) + time (0.28 × 30.00 min = $8.40) = $25.70, multiplied by the 1.6 surge you both accept ($41.12), plus the $0.80 platform fee and the $2.50 Kim Keat Link gantry that lies on the optimal route = recomputed_fare $44.42. Charged total was $58.10. On the separate lines the ruling rests on: charged_total $58.10, recomputed_fare $44.42, refund $13.68, rounded up to $13.70. That is above the $0.50 de minimis floor and 23.5% of the charge, far below the 90% share that would convert this to a full refund.\n\nOn the ERP: only the $2.50 Kim Keat Link gantry lies on the optimal route. The $2.00 Adam Road gantry is off-route, but it is already comprehended in the $44.42 recomputed fare and must not be added on top (POL-RD-09(1)); it is itemised here for transparency only. Both gantries are genuine crossings — the trace passes within 0.0 m and 8.76 m of them, inside the 250 m match — so there is no phantom line, no billing-integrity correction and no referral under POL-RD-09(4).\n\nPOL-RD-06 is not engaged and no driver-conduct referral arises: this deviation is not material, and in any event no repeat pattern is established on the only citable counters — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1 over 412 completed trips is 0.002 (below 0.05). The refund is well below the $150.00 escalation ceiling. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, all three artifacts carry trip_id TRP-00114, the trace is unimpaired (241 fixes, 10-second interval, zero gaps), the timestamps agree, and every billed line has a counterpart in the trace."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's explanation — 'AYE was crawling from the Alexandra exit' — is, under POL-RD-13, tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else. The only advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00114-01, is MISSING: it has no payload and weight_multiplier 0.0. I disclose that impairment and cite the artifact for its absence, not its content. With no advisory record, POL-RD-03's comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the congestion assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00114-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The absent advisory is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The driver names no evidence ID for any advisory — his statement says only 'No advisory that I know of'. Under POL-RD-13(1) an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one, so this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact. POL-RD-10(5) does not fire, and the case should be ruled on rather than escalated.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00114-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}

