    "explanation": "Both parties agree on the substance, and the evidence supports the rider's core point. Measured the way POL-RD-01 requires — from gps_trace.trace_distance_km of 23.97 km, not the rounded 24.0 km convenience copy on the trip record — against the booked optimal of 18.00 km, the excess is 5.97 km, or 33.17% of optimal. Both establishment gates pass (above 20% and above 0.8 km), so the route deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not MATERIAL: 33.17% is under the 50% gate and 5.97 km is under the 8.0 km gate, so the POL-RD-06 FULL_REFUND uplift and the POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral do not arise; the profile check fails in any event (deviation_flags_90d is 1, below 3; 1/412 completed trips = 0.002, below 0.05). Neither advocate pressed that limb. The trace is clean for policy purposes — 241 fixes at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gaps, max inter-fix gap 0 s — so POL-RD-07(a)–(c) is not met and no independent corroboration is required; the driver's chat message and his filed statement conceding the PIE routing are therefore not needed to carry the finding. The driver's congestion account does not change the result. No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-00114-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so the POL-RD-03 comparison cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver names no advisory identifier, POL-RD-13(1) applies and this gap in the bundle is a missing proof, not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The other exculpatory limbs are checked and none applies: no rider instruction in the chat and both waypoint_hint fields null (POL-RD-04); no pickup or dropoff amendment (POL-RD-05); fare model METERED, not UPFRONT_QUOTE (POL-RD-11); vehicle type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12). The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, run on the METERED model: charged_total 58.10; recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 18.00 + 0.28 x 30.00) x 1.6 = 41.12, plus the 0.80 platform fee and the 2.50 ERP on the optimal route (Kim Keat Link), giving 44.42; refund = 58.10 - 44.42 = 13.68, rounded up to 13.70. The 1.6 surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, where the policy says it lives, and applied only to base, distance and time and not to ERP — so none of the surge you accepted is clawed back. On ERP: the 2.50 Kim Keat Link gantry lies on the optimal route and sits inside the recomputed fare; the 2.00 Adam Road gantry is off-route but is already comprehended in the 13.70 under POL-RD-09(1) and is not added on top. Neither is a phantom line — the trace passes within 0 m and 8.76 m respectively, well inside the 250 m match — so no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral arises. 13.68 is above the 0.50 de minimis floor and is 23.5% of the charge, below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a partial refund. No POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, the trace is unimpaired, timestamps agree, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a cited missing artifact, both charge lines are matched to the trace, and the refund is far below the 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total. The rider is refunded SGD 13.70 of the 15.00 contested; the driver receives no compensation."
